			"type": "group",
			"x": 20,
			"y": 670,
			"width": 1880,
			"height": 510,
			"label": "Simulation API"
		},
		{
			"id": "group-loggin",
			"type": "group",
			"x": 20,
			"y": 1300,
			"width": 1880,
			"height": 510,
			"label": "Logging Viz"
		},
		{
			"id": "group-script",
			"type": "group",
			"x": 20,
			"y": 2810,
			"width": 1880,
			"height": 510,
			"label": "Scripts UX"
		},
		{
			"id": "legend",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "## Legend\n🔴 **Red** = To Do (ready)\n⬜ **Gray** = Blocked\n🟠 **Orange** = Doing\n🔵 **Cyan** = Ready to review\n🟢 **Green** = Done\n🟣 **Purple** = Proposed by agent",
			"x": -540,
			"y": -310,
			"width": 380,
			"height": 230,
			"color": "0"
		},
		{
			"id": "canvas-warnings",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "## Warnings\n✓ None",
			"x": -540,
			"y": -530,
			"width": 380,
			"height": 200,
			"color": "3"
		},
		{
			"id": "canvas-errors",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "## Errors\n✓ None",
			"x": -540,
			"y": -750,
			"width": 380,
			"height": 200,
			"color": "1"
		},
		{
			"id": "287c55df",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "## SA-01 Define observation contract\nDesign a real observation schema, populate observation_space, and document the intended public control-step interface versus internal microphysics stepping.",
			"x": 80,
			"y": 710,
			"width": 420,
			"height": 180,
			"color": "6"
		},
		{
			"id": "bc77ad27",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "## PM-01 Respect zero-valued generator commands\n\nReplaced truthy fallback checks in ignition with explicit None handling so 0V and 0us commands are preserved instead of snapping back to defaults. Added regression coverage that proves None still falls back while explicit zero-valued target voltage, ON time, and OFF time remain zero.",
			"x": 80,
			"y": 1970,
			"width": 420,
			"height": 190,
			"color": "4"
		},
		{
			"id": "fb7f612e",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "## PM-02 Align module default discharge settings\n\nAligned ignition and material fallback handling around a shared crater-backed default current mode in the env. Reset and missing/unsupported state current modes now resolve to the same physical discharge mode, and regression tests cover both None and unsupported-mode fallbacks.",
			"x": 1420,
			"y": 1970,
			"width": 420,
			"height": 250,
			"color": "4"
		},
		{
			"id": "dfc7eb85",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "## PM-03 Make dt handling coherent\nAudit timestep scaling across ignition, wire, dielectric, and mechanics; either fully support variable dt or validate dt==1 and remove the misleading configurability.",
			"x": 80,
			"y": 2220,
			"width": 420,
			"height": 180,
			"color": "6"
		},
		{
			"id": "ba618130",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "## PM-04 Clarify mechanics and constraint semantics\nDocumented position-control semantics in MechanicsModule docstring. Removed three orphaned EnvironmentConfig fields (max_wire_temperature, min_gap_for_operation, max_cutting_force) that were never enforced. Updated docs.",
			"x": 80,
			"y": 2440,
			"width": 420,
			"height": 200,
			"color": "5"
		},
		{
			"id": "8ac634f4",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "## SA-02 Refactor public step contract\nMake every public step consume an action and return a valid observation and reward, even if the environment internally substeps physics for servo or discharge timing.",
			"x": 750,
			"y": 710,
			"width": 420,
			"height": 180,
			"color": "6"
		},
		{
			"id": "98a5aab4",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "## SA-03 Redesign current-mode action encoding\nReplace the current_mode Box(1..19) with an encoding that only represents supported crater-data modes so sampled actions are valid by construction.",
			"x": 80,
			"y": 960,
			"width": 420,
			"height": 180,
			"color": "6"
		},
		{
			"id": "0d1a98c9",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "## SA-04 Finalize RL semantics and compliance tests\nImplement non-placeholder reward and truncation semantics, then add Gym-style contract tests for reset/step formats, valid sampled actions, and wrapper compatibility.",
			"x": 1420,
			"y": 710,
			"width": 420,
			"height": 180,
			"color": "6"
		},
		{
			"id": "280b5854",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "## LV-04 Make analysis tracking opt-in and reset-safe\nGate crater-history and other analysis-only accumulators behind explicit configuration and make sure they reset cleanly between episodes.",
			"x": 1420,
			"y": 1590,
			"width": 420,
			"height": 180,
			"color": "6"
		},
		{
			"id": "5f202c6f",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "## LV-01 Promote wire diagnostics into the state contract\nMove wire_head_idx, wire_offset_mm, wire_material_positions_mm, and similar diagnostics into EDMState or a formal derived-signal registry instead of dynamic attribute writes.",
			"x": 80,
			"y": 1340,
			"width": 420,
			"height": 250,
			"color": "6"
		},
		{
			"id": "4b9517d0",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "## LV-02 Repair logger and export contracts\nUpdate SimulationLogger validation, exporters, and dashboard pack metadata so visualization-required signals are supported without bypassing the type contract.",
			"x": 750,
			"y": 1340,
			"width": 420,
			"height": 180,
			"color": "6"
		},
		{
			"id": "217e4253",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "## PC-03 Split fast and slow test lanes\nSeparate long stochastic physics tests from the default fast suite, add example and logging smoke tests, and keep CI runtime practical.",
			"x": 2090,
			"y": 3480,
			"width": 420,
			"height": 180,
			"color": "6"
		},
		{
			"id": "370962f7",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "## PC-01 Remove duplicate wire state sync\nStop synchronizing both dataclass Segment objects and NumPy arrays every microstep unless a consumer actually needs both views.",
			"x": 80,
			"y": 3480,
			"width": 420,
			"height": 180,
			"color": "6"
		},
		{
			"id": "b253d8f3",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "## PC-02 Accelerate thermal and damage hot paths\nVectorize or compile the per-segment damage loop and decide whether to delete or finally use the dead thermal-update kernel so the code path matches the intended optimization story.",
			"x": 750,
			"y": 3480,
			"width": 420,
			"height": 180,
			"color": "6"
		},
		{
			"id": "3a258c06",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "## SU-01 Repair example runner configs\nUpdate examples/quickstart.py and examples/run_simulation.py to use the current logger signal names and a working end-to-end export path.",
			"x": 1420,
			"y": 2850,
			"width": 420,
			"height": 180,
			"color": "6"
		},
		{
			"id": "27ab8b1b",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "## SU-03 Fix voltage sweep experiment semantics\nFixed voltage sweep semantics in experiments/voltage_sweep_speed_analysis.py: (1) generator_control.target_voltage now follows the swept setpoint (was hardcoded 80 V). (2) Thermal quench uses WireModuleParameters.base_convection_coefficient=1e8; removed no-op env.wire.h_conv. (3) Wire diameter set on EnvironmentConfig.wire_diameter=0.25 mm (was invalid wire_params.wire_diameter). (4) Plot/npz aligned with protocol: x-axis target voltage, dropped misleading SSoil/ssoll; npz no longer writes ssoll_values.",
			"x": 80,
			"y": 2850,
			"width": 420,
			"height": 215,
			"color": "4"
		},
		{
			"id": "5f730cee",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "## SU-04 Normalize CLI output portability\nReplaced all non-ASCII glyphs in print() output across canvas-tool.py and experiment scripts with ASCII-safe equivalents: arrows -> ->, checkmarks -> [ok], crosses -> [FAIL], warning emoji -> [!], em dashes -> --, micro sign -> u, superscripts -> ^^, middle dots -> *.",
			"x": 80,
			"y": 3100,
			"width": 420,
			"height": 180,
			"color": "5"
		},
		{
			"id": "2288b93e",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "## SU-02 Repair experiment logging workflows\nFix experiments/run_simulation.py and related animation entry points so their default logging modes run successfully without requiring --no-log.",
			"x": 1420,
			"y": 3100,
			"width": 420,
			"height": 180,
			"color": "6"
		},
		{
			"id": "aa2748ce",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "## PC-04 Make pytest work from a clean checkout\nConfigure the test runner so pytest can import wedm without manual PYTHONPATH setup, matching contributor and CI expectations.",
			"x": 80,
			"y": 3730,
			"width": 420,
			"height": 180,
			"color": "6"
		},
		{
			"id": "eda4ab9f",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "## ES-03 Define episode-start defaults\nApply a single source of truth for initial generator, thermal, and electrical state so the first environment step does not depend on stale internals or mismatched per-module fallbacks.",
			"x": 750,
			"y": 330,
			"width": 420,
			"height": 180,
			"color": "4"
		},
		{
			"id": "5733330b",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "## ES-04 Add reset isolation tests",
			"x": 1420,
			"y": 80,
			"width": 420,
			"height": 180,
			"color": "4"
		},
		{
			"id": "d8acd2df",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "## ES-02 Reset internal thermal and analysis state\nExpanded the module reset hooks so they now synchronize their mirrored EDMState fields as well as private caches. Ignition clears spark/current short state, dielectric clears debris and ion-channel state, mechanics clears servo carry-over, and wire clears the broken flag; regression coverage now verifies reset hooks work even on a dirty existing state object.",
			"x": 750,
			"y": 80,
			"width": 420,
			"height": 180,
			"color": "4"
		},
		{
			"id": "aeddc858",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "## ES-01 Add module reset hooks\nIntroduce a formal reset API on ignition, wire, material, dielectric, and mechanics modules and call it from WireEDMEnv.reset so internal caches and episodic state cannot leak between runs.",
			"x": 80,
			"y": 80,
			"width": 420,
			"height": 180,
			"color": "4"
		},
		{
			"id": "d84a8af7",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "## LV-03 Add end-to-end logging smoke tests\nAdd NPZ/pack generation tests that assert dashboard-required fields exist and can be exported from a real environment run.",
			"x": 1420,
			"y": 1340,
			"width": 420,
			"height": 180,
			"color": "6"
		}
	],
